
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F G : Points
D,A,B are collinear [00]
CD ⟂ AB [01]
E,A,C are collinear [02]
BE ⟂ AC [03]
F,C,B are collinear [04]
FC = FB [05]
GD = GE [06]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. A,D,B are collinear [00] & CD ⟂ AB [01] ⇒  CD ⟂ DB [07]
002. F,C,B are collinear [04] & FC = FB [05] ⇒  F is midpoint of CB [08]
003. CD ⟂ DB [07] & F is midpoint of CB [08] ⇒  CF = DF [09]
004. E,A,C are collinear [02] & AC ⟂ BE [03] ⇒  CE ⟂ EB [10]
005. CE ⟂ EB [10] & F is midpoint of CB [08] ⇒  CF = EF [11]
006. CF = DF [09] & CF = EF [11] ⇒  FE = FD [12]
007. FE = FD [12] & GD = GE [06] ⇒  DE ⟂ FG
==========================
